Silven Grayson is a sharp-dressed human male in his mid-twenties, inheriting the family's striking stark-white hair and cool slate-gray eyes, immaculate in amber-and-black formal wear with a subtle stylized pulse motif stitched into the lining.

Silven is a member of [[Org/Amber Call/index|Amber Call]]. He came aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] for the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] with [[Org/Pale Lantern Society/People/Manus Sudrenus|Manus Sudrenus]] and [[Org/NecroLog/People/Gaspar Caetano|Gaspar Caetano]], and when the tear opened in the banquet floor he bent one of the Ki-Rin to his will and drew his people off the floor. Afterwards he and Manus were seen treating the barghest corpses with alchemical reagents. He is personable and keeps a friendly face, and politely declined [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s offer of healing.

He keeps his hands clean in public, and those who watch him closely do not trust the act. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] saw him turn a Ki-Rin against the guests and go for a kill in the confusion, and called it out; [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Bishop]] of the [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] knows of it and says it cannot be pressed in public for want of proof.

Since the Providence halted he has held the ground nearest the void creatures' holes. He sent a bone drone to the Party's gate with a note asking to parlay, and met them at [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Giacomo's|Giacomo's]] with [[Org/Iridescent Church/People/Walter Stoke|Walter Stoke]] and [[Org/Ministry of Cultural Progress/People/Giannos Hasikos|Giannos]]. He agreed to a truce: no fighting in the central circle, no crossing of one another's ground, and notes left and answered at Giacomo's, which he means to keep unchanged. The void creatures do not come at him, and he would not say why. In return for the Party's news that the strider had stood on this world before, he told them the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] had done the pilgrimage's work for a thing outside the firmament called [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]], and that War's liaison had come to his family with the same offer, and been refused.
